!!<*yamlover: $defs: chapter>
As bytes a format decodes
description: file/binary plus a format — the meta says how to read the value
- >
  A scalar may live as raw bytes: a `file/binary` member whose `meta.yo` entry gives the decoding —
  `type: binary` with `format: int32/le` turns a four-byte file into an integer; `image/png` keeps an
  image an image. The data is the on-disk file; the metadata says how to read it — the instance and
  its description never trade places ([metadata first](::language:principles:metadata-first)).
